      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T00:14:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I assume that it is okay if `MakeFromStream` may fail (returning `kIncompleteInput`) if the input stream doesn\u0027t yet cover `IHDR` chunk.  IIUC the GIF decoder follows the same behavior.\n\nIn practice `MakeStream` needs to build a color profile and therefore it may need to decode everything until the first `IDAT` chunk.  I assume that this is also okay - there doesn\u0027t seem to be a way around this (since `SkCodec` takes `SkEncodedInfo` as a parameter and `SkEncodedInfo` needs to take into account `gAMA`, `iCCP`, etc.).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 93,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "9462c01701c55c934255e1a6d9f843923a79d760",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
